\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Fine sites in two dimensions}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{For #{n=2}, the [fine-site map](fdip-014V) sends the
vertex at #{x} to the even-even site #{2x}. The two edges
based there go to #{2x+(1,0)} and #{2x+(0,1)}, and their
face goes to #{2x+(1,1)}. The cells occupy all 4
corners of a unit fine square. For example, the right endpoint
of the first edge is at #{2x+(2,0)}. At the last coarse
column this is the vertex in the first fine column, since
the fine first period is #{2N_1}.}
